From 0248570b172c64f05d3c5b701c19d03f08c13784 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 12:42:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: drop the steps auditing code that no longer exists; make
 Docker prove itself
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three rounds of deletion left CI auditing things that are gone.

Session 74 deleted assets/js/ (119,698 lines, reachable only from
tests/archive/). Five workflows still pointed at it; deploy.yml's
`find assets/js -name "vr-*.js"` exits 1, so that job could only fail.

Then tools/benchmark.js and its regression checker went. They timed
require() of files under assets/js/, so once that tree was gone the tool
found zero modules and crashed in its own summary — the job running it
was permanently red while saying nothing about the code, and the
regression checker compared against a baseline file not in the repo.
Removed: benchmark.yml entirely, ci.yml's Performance Tests job (and its
entries in the summary job), and release.yml's benchmark step. Size is
measured instead, by tools/check-bundle-size.mjs, which budgets the
gzipped chunks that ship and runs inside `npm run gate`.

Then Prettier. `npm run format:check` had never passed. Running
`npm run format` to find out why turned over 127 files (+6,016/-3,990)
and took ESLint from 0 errors to 195, because `indent: ["error", 2]` and
Prettier disagree. It was a standard declared in package.json and never
applied, whose adoption would damage the one that is enforced, so it was
removed from the repo; ESLint is the formatter of record. Its steps go
with it, and ESLint loses `continue-on-error` in the same breath — it is
green, so there is no reason left to swallow its result.

The Docker job is strengthened rather than removed. Its only assertion
was `curl -f /health`, which nginx.conf answers with a static 200
regardless of the document root — so it stayed green while the image
served unbuilt src/. (Measured by reproducing the image's document root
and loading it in Chromium: window.QuiBrowser undefined, uncaught
"TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'PROD')", since
import.meta.env is substituted at build time and never existed there.)
The Dockerfile now builds, and this job checks the served page is the
built bundle and that raw source is NOT reachable.

Also deletes wasm-build.yml and v5.8.0-planning.yml, both of which only
built or audited assets/js/. wasm-build.yml was additionally malformed
YAML at line 178. Every remaining workflow parses, checked with
yaml.safe_load.

Nothing in .github/workflows/ now references assets/js/, tools/benchmark.js,
check-performance-regression.js, or prettier.

This is supplied as a patch because the agent's token lacks the
`workflows` permission; pushes touching .github/workflows/** return 403,
measured over git and the REST API. Apply with `git am`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
